  "facts": [
    "Oławski Bridge, built 1882‑83 by Alexander Kaumann, stretches 73.8 meters across the Oława River, its brick arches crowned with hammered stone blocks that echo Baroque elegance.",
    "The bridge’s ornate railings feature balusters modeled after Baroque iconography, while Gustav Trelenberg’s metal decorations, crafted under P. Heisler and Robert Toberentza, add a sculptural flourish.",
    "Renovated twice—once in 1962 and again in 1990—Oławski Bridge survived wartime upheaval, even once carrying a tram line before the tracks were removed during a later overhaul."
